# Environment for the image smoke test (docker/smoke.sh, run by the `images` job of
# .github/workflows/ci.yaml and by .github/workflows/docker.yaml before an image is pushed).
# Placeholder values only: the container must boot and answer /healthz without any real
# infrastructure behind it. Never put real credentials here. The other checks of the smoke test
# (users, files in the image, the migration command) start no service and need no environment.
#
# When a service gains a variable that it requires at startup, add a placeholder for it here (the
# test fails with the service's own "Invalid environment" message otherwise). If a service ever
# needs a live dependency just to boot, extend the smoke job to start it instead.
LOG_LEVEL=info
